{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request e224cc00: yes. G1 adds `resolveJsonModule: true`\nto exactly these seven compiler configurations:\n\n- packages/derive/tsconfig.test.json\n- packages/platform/tsconfig.test.json\n- packages/cli/tsconfig.json\n- packages/cli/tsconfig.scope.json\n- apps/room/page/tsconfig.test.json\n- apps/room/page/tsconfig.scope.json\n- scripts/tsconfig.json\n\nThe option follows from ruling on 361bb699: a runtime export reads\nthe generated JSON and takes its type by a type-only import. Nine\nconfigurations on main already set it.\n\nLimits:\n1. The edit sets that one option and changes no other. Every strict\n   option, assertion and retained pin stays.\n2. No production configuration of contract, bytes or derive gains\n   the option. The kernel packages import no JSON at run time. The\n   kernel boundary check stays as it is.\n3. If the focused compiler closure names one more context that\n   lacks the option, add it there under this ruling and list it in\n   the head report. Do not ask again.\n\nThe implementation note lists the configurations and says which\nimport in each needs the option.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}